        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "• BERT is a model that fine-tunes the pre-trained BERT $ ^{15} $ (Devlin et al., 2019) and estimates the emotional intensity as  $ y = \\text{softmax}(hW) $, where  $ h $ is a feature vector obtained for the [CLS] token of BERT. We investigate the performance of both BERT trained with subjective labels (Subj. BERT) and BERT trained with objective labels (Obj.",
